Yambo build provenance
======================

The release version (for example 5.4.0) remains in
include/version/version.m4.  The identity of compiled source is generated by
make and is not maintained by a Git hook.

sbin/generate_build_provenance.sh writes two content-stable files:

  include/version/build_provenance.h
  config/build-provenance.txt

In an out-of-tree build these paths are in the build tree.  The header is
embedded by the common driver library.  After linking, the manifest is also
copied next to each executable as <executable>.provenance.  It contains no
timestamp, hostname, or local path.

Data sources, in precedence order, are explicit YAMBO_BUILD_* environment
variables, the local Git checkout, include/version/release_provenance.txt,
and explicit unknown values.  The supported overrides are:

  YAMBO_BUILD_COMMIT
  YAMBO_BUILD_REF
  YAMBO_BUILD_TAG
  YAMBO_BUILD_DIRTY (clean/dirty, yes/no, true/false, or 1/0)
  YAMBO_BUILD_SOURCE

Release archives should include include/version/release_provenance.txt using
the same key=value format as config/build-provenance.txt.  Release automation
must write the full commit, exact tag, state=clean, and
source=release-manifest before creating the archive.  CI may instead provide
all values through the environment, which avoids requiring .git on an HPC
build host.

Only tracked changes, staged or unstaged, make a Git build dirty.  Untracked
build products are deliberately ignored.  The full commit is authoritative;
the abbreviated commit and ref are display fields.  The historical Revision
value remains in the ABI for compatibility but is not build provenance.

